The first test (`should answer the first question`) sets a property in localStorage. The second test (`should pre-fill the first question when going back`) reads the data from localStorage as part of pre-filling the question answer. After a couple of days we found out that localStorage data is cleared between tests. At that point we also thought that clearing between tests meant between each end-to-end test, but it happens more often (between every `it`).

By adding the line `Cypress.LocalStorage.clear = function(keys, ls, rs){};` at the top of the test it's solved, since localStorage clearing doesn't happen anymore, but the default behaviour of clearing it between test cases caused quite some time and frustration for us in trying to figure out what was going wrong, and raises the question whether this should be the default behaviour.

