# Solution

As I mentioned in the comment below, I came up with the following solution:

I figured out how to do this using `cy.then()`

You can do it in one function:
```
Cypress.Commands.add("loginAndSaveSession", () => {
  cy.then(() => AuthLib.signIn(username, password)).then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```

or with two functions:
```
Cypress.Commands.add("login", () => {
  return AuthLib.signIn(username, password);
});

Cypress.Commands.add("loginAndSaveSession", () => {
  cy.login().then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```

You can find an example here: [https://github.com/Nxtra/cypress-amplify-auth-test/blob/main/cypress/support/commands.js](https://github.com/Nxtra/cypress-amplify-auth-test/blob/main/cypress/support/commands.js)
And some explanation here: [https://www.theclouddeveloper.io/use-cypress-to-test-aws-amplify-apps-with-authentication](https://www.theclouddeveloper.io/use-cypress-to-test-aws-amplify-apps-with-authentication)

